## 1. Boston Marriott Copley Place  
**Address:** 200 Huntington Ave, Boston, MA 02116  
**Distance to BCEC:** ~1.2 km (≈ 0.8 mi) – a 5‑minute walk or a 2‑minute taxi ride.  

### Why it’s a good fit
| Feature | Details |
|---------|---------|
| **Room options** | *Standard King* (king‑size bed) or *Two‑Double* – both provide a spacious work desk and free high‑speed Wi‑Fi. |
| **Business amenities** | 24‑hour business centre, meeting rooms, and ample power outlets. |
| **On‑site facilities** | Fitness centre, rooftop lounge with city views, and a full‑service restaurant (The Bistro). |
| **Convenience** | Directly connected to the **Copley Place** shopping mall – easy for quick meals, coffee, or a quiet spot to review papers. |
| **Typical nightly rate (2024‑25 season)** | **≈ $210–$260** for a standard king room (rates vary with corporate/academic discounts). |

---

## 2. The Westin Boston Seaport District  
**Address:** 425 Summer St, Boston, MA 02210  
**Distance to BCEC:** ~1.6 km (≈ 1 mi) – a 5‑minute drive or a pleasant 10‑minute walk along the Seaport promenade.  

### Why it’s a good fit
| Feature | Details |
|---------|---------|
| **Room options** | *Westin King* (signature “Heavenly Bed”) or *Westin Twin* – both include a large work desk and ergonomic chair. |
| **Business amenities** | WestinWORKOUT® gym, 24‑hour business centre, and complimentary high‑speed Wi‑Fi throughout the hotel. |
| **On‑site facilities** | Rooftop bar with harbor views, on‑site restaurant (The Barking Crab) serving fresh New England seafood, and a spa for post‑conference relaxation. |
| **Eco‑friendly design** | Floor‑to‑ceiling windows and sustainable building features create a bright, healthy work environment. |
| **Typical nightly rate** | **≈ $230–$280** for a king‑bed room. |

---

## 3. Hyatt Regency Boston  
**Address:** 1 Avenue de Lafayette, Boston, MA 02111  
**Distance to BCEC:** ~2.0 km (≈ 1.2 mi) – a 6‑minute drive or a 12‑minute walk via the Harborwalk.  

### Why it’s a good fit
| Feature | Details |
|---------|---------|
| **Room options** | *Deluxe King* or *Deluxe Twin* – each room offers a king‑size bed, a dedicated work desk, and a large bathroom with a separate shower. |
| **Direct BCEC access** | Linked to the convention center by a covered sky‑walk (the “BCEC‑Hyatt” connector) – you can step out of the lobby and be at the symposium in seconds. |
| **Business amenities** | 24‑hour business centre, meeting rooms, and robust high‑speed internet. |
| **On‑site facilities** | Harbor Club lounge, rooftop bar with panoramic harbor views, fitness centre, and several dining options (including a steakhouse and a casual café). |
| **Typical nightly rate** | **≈ $220–$270** for a deluxe king room. |

---

## Quick Booking Checklist

| Item | Details |
|------|---------|
| **Check‑in** | 15:00 on Nov 25 2024 |
| **Check‑out** | 11:00 on Nov 30 2024 |
| **Rooms needed** | 2 rooms (each for 2 adults) – request **non‑smoking** and **quiet** rooms for a focused work environment. |
| **Special requests** | • Early check‑in / late check‑out (if travel schedule requires it). <br>• High‑speed Wi‑Fi and a desk in each room (standard at all three hotels). |
| **Transportation** | All three hotels are a short taxi/ rideshare ride from the BCEC. The Westin and Hyatt are also reachable via the **Silver Line SL1** (Boston Logan‑Airport‑to‑Seaport) and the **T (Red Line)** – convenient if you prefer public transit. |
| **Cancellation policy** | Most Boston hotels allow free cancellation up to 48 hours before arrival – verify when you book. |
| **Potential discounts** | Mention that you’re a research group attending a symposium; many hotels offer modest academic or group‑rate discounts. |

